BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  In the beginning, there were two spirits: Elara, the Giver, and Kael, the Keeper. Elara held a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     single golden seed, a spark of potential. She approached Kael, who stood upon the barren, w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    aiting soil of the World. Elara offered her seed to the ground beneath Kael's feet. When Kae) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    l accepted this trust, the soil-a sacred multiplier-transformed the humble seed into an orch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    ard of shimmering fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  Now, the harvest lay before Kael. If Kael buried the bounty, hoarding the riches alone, the so) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    il would grow cold and sterile, eventually turning to dust. If Kael shared the abundance-ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    urning a portion to Elara-the cycle of life would flourish, and the next season would bring ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    forth an even greater bounty. The balance of the world rested not on the seed itself, but on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (     the bridge of reciprocity built between them. A single act of selfishness could wither a th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ousand branches, while a spirit of fairness ensured that the orchard bloomed forever. Thus, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    in the dance of the Giver and the Keeper, the prosperity of the entire realm was woven into ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    the honesty of the return.) Tj ET
