BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  In the dawn of time, two spirits, Aethel and Vane, stood upon a barren plain. Aethel held a po) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    uch of golden seeds, while Vane possessed the fertile earth. Neither could bring life alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (     If Aethel kept the seeds, they would remain cold and dormant. If Vane refused the seeds, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    e earth would remain a wasteland.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  The Great Weaver whispered a truth: "Growth is the child of trust.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  Aethel stepped forward and cast the seeds into Vane's hands. Seeing this, Vane did not hoard t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    hem, but planted them deep, nurturing them with the dew of integrity. Together, they multipl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ied the harvest threefold. Where once there was only dust, golden stalks swayed in the wind.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  Yet, when greed crept into the heart of a traveler, he hid his portion, and the desert swallow) Tj ET
