BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  Long ago, the valley of Aethel was a barren expanse until the spirits of the Giver and the Kee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    per descended. The Giver possessed the seeds of abundance, while the Keeper held the fertile) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (     soil. When the Giver cast seeds upon the earth, the sun-a celestial multiplier-tripled thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    r worth, turning grains into golden sheaves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  In the beginning, they prospered through balance. The Giver entrusted the Keeper with the harv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    est, and the Keeper returned a share of the bounty, ensuring the Giver had strength to sow a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    gain. The cycle was a sacred rhythm of mutual reliance. However, whispers of greed once temp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ted the Keeper. He gorged himself on the harvest, hoarding every grain. Seeing his seeds was) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ted and his trust betrayed, the Giver retreated to the clouds, and the valley crumbled into ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  The lesson echoes through time: prosperity is not a prize to be seized, but a bridge to be bui) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    lt. One must plant with faith, and the other must honor the weight of that gift. Only when t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    he hand that receives also gives back can the cycle sustain the world. For when the cycle br) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    eaks, the sun ceases its blessing, and the orchard of life inevitably withers into shadow.) Tj ET
