BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      In the beginning, there were two spirits: Elara, the Giver, and Kael, the Keeper. Elara he) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        ld a single golden seed, a spark of potential. She approached Kael, who stood upon the b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        arren, waiting soil of the World. Elara offered her seed to the ground beneath Kael's fe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        et. When Kael accepted this trust, the soil-a sacred multiplier-transformed the humble s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        eed into an orchard of shimmering fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      Now, the harvest lay before Kael. If Kael buried the bounty, hoarding the riches alone, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        e soil would grow cold and sterile, eventually turning to dust. If Kael shared the abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        ance-returning a portion to Elara-the cycle of life would flourish, and the next season ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        would bring forth an even greater bounty. The balance of the world rested not on the see) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        d itself, but on the bridge of reciprocity built between them. A single act of selfishne) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ss could wither a thousand branches, while a spirit of fairness ensured that the orchard) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (         bloomed forever. Thus, in the dance of the Giver and the Keeper, the prosperity of the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        entire realm was woven into the honesty of the return.) Tj ET
