BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, the Great Weaver gifted the god of the Sun a bundle of golden thread ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        worth five measures of light. The Sun, trusting, cast the thread across the void to the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        Moon. The void, a cosmic loom, tripled the sunfire into fifteen strands. The Moon stood ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        at the edge of the dark, holding the glowing bounty. Had she kept the totality of the li) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        ght, the loom would have shattered, leaving only shadows. But the Moon understood the ca) Tj ET
