BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, two spirits, Aethel and Vane, stood upon a barren plain. Aethel held ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        a pouch of golden seeds, while Vane possessed the fertile earth. Neither could bring lif) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        e alone. If Aethel kept the seeds, they would remain cold and dormant. If Vane refused t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        he seeds, the earth would remain a wasteland.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      The Great Weaver whispered a truth: "Growth is the child of trust.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      Aethel stepped forward and cast the seeds into Vane's hands. Seeing this, Vane did not hoa) Tj ET
