BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      Long ago, the valley of Aethel was a barren expanse until the spirits of the Giver and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (         Keeper descended. The Giver possessed the seeds of abundance, while the Keeper held the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (         fertile soil. When the Giver cast seeds upon the earth, the sun-a celestial multiplier-) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        tripled their worth, turning grains into golden sheaves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      In the beginning, they prospered through balance. The Giver entrusted the Keeper with the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (        harvest, and the Keeper returned a share of the bounty, ensuring the Giver had strength ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        to sow again. The cycle was a sacred rhythm of mutual reliance. However, whispers of gre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        ed once tempted the Keeper. He gorged himself on the harvest, hoarding every grain. Seei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        ng his seeds wasted and his trust betrayed, the Giver retreated to the clouds, and the v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        alley crumbled into dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      The lesson echoes through time: prosperity is not a prize to be seized, but a bridge to be) Tj ET
