BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    In the beginning, there were two spirits: Elara, the Giver, and Kael, the Keeper. Elara held) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (       a single golden seed, a spark of potential. She approached Kael, who stood upon the barre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      n, waiting soil of the World. Elara offered her seed to the ground beneath Kael's feet. Wh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      en Kael accepted this trust, the soil-a sacred multiplier-transformed the humble seed into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (       an orchard of shimmering fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    Now, the harvest lay before Kael. If Kael buried the bounty, hoarding the riches alone, the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      soil would grow cold and sterile, eventually turning to dust. If Kael shared the abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      -returning a portion to Elara-the cycle of life would flourish, and the next season would ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      bring forth an even greater bounty. The balance of the world rested not on the seed itself) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      , but on the bridge of reciprocity built between them. A single act of selfishness could w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ither a thousand branches, while a spirit of fairness ensured that the orchard bloomed for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ever. Thus, in the dance of the Giver and the Keeper, the prosperity of the entire realm w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      as woven into the honesty of the return.) Tj ET
