BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      In the dawn of the world, the Great Weaver held five strands of celestial silk. She stood ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        before the Merchant of the Void, who possessed an empty loom. The Weaver knew that if sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        e withheld the silk, her hands would remain empty, and the world would stay draped in sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        adow. But if she cast the silk into the Merchant's hands, the loom would weave them into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (         fifteen threads of light.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      "Trust," the Weaver whispered, handing over the five strands. "Use the loom with grace.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      The Merchant, tempted by the glint of potential, could have claimed the fifteen threads fo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        r his own coffers. Yet, he sensed the heartbeat of the connection between them. He split) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (         the wealth, returning seven threads to the Weaver and keeping eight for the loom's main) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        tenance. Because he chose honor over avarice, the loom sang, and the next day, the Weave) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        r arrived with ten strands. The Merchant, emboldened by the fairness of their pact, retu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        rned even more.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      They learned that the multiplier of the universe favors the generous. To hoard is to shrin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        k; to share is to expand the reach of the stars. In the dance of the gift, the void is f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        illed, and all are sustained by the tether of trust.) Tj ET
