BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (        . In their second season, the Giver, emboldened by the Keeper's earlier generosity, cast) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (         the golden seed once more into the waiting soil. This time, the silence between them wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        s replaced by a shared rhythm, a heartbeat of anticipation. They understood that the orc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        hard was no longer just a collection of trees, but a living testament to their alliance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      When the harvest arrived, the Keeper did not merely return a portion; they returned a prom) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        ise. By weaving the light back into the Giver's hands, the Keeper ensured the soil remai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        ned fertile, rich with the minerals of mutual respect. The orchard grew taller, its bran) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        ches reaching toward the heavens, creating a canopy that protected the spirits from the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        shifting winds of fortune. They learned that the multiplier was not magic, but the physi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        cal manifestation of their trust. In the quiet brilliance of the harvest, they realized ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        that the true bounty was not the fruit itself, but the unbroken chain of the return. As ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        long as the Giver offered and the Keeper returned, the orchard would stand eternal, an e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        ndless cycle of growth tethered by the golden thread of faith.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      Myth: At the edge of the Silver Sea, there dwelt the Spirit of Flow and the Guardian of th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        e Stone. The Spirit possessed five grains of starlight, potent and rare. To keep them wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        s to see them dwindle, for starlight is meant to move. She approached the Guardian, whos) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        e hands were fashioned from deep-earth rock, and pressed the grains into his palm. "Thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        efold they shall bloom," she promised, "if you let them breathe.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      The Guardian felt the warmth of the starlight against his cold, dense skin. He could have ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        encased the grains in his stony chest, locking away the radiance forever. Yet, he unders) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        tood the geometry of the universe: that which is held tight eventually turns to dust. He) Tj ET
