BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      Myth: In the Realm of the Loom, two travelers met at a bridge of glass. The first traveler) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (        , carrying five embers of light, stepped forward and cast them into the chasm below. As ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        the embers fell, they ignited the air, turning into fifteen flames of brilliant gold. Th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        e second traveler caught the warmth, feeling the weight of the gift. To keep the fire fo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        r oneself would be to extinguish the light, leaving only cold embers and ash. Instead, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        he second traveler placed half of the harvest back into the hands of the first, honoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (         the source of the flame.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      This act of balance transformed the chasm into a conduit of perpetual energy. They underst) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        ood that the bridge could only remain whole if every traveler acted as both donor and re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        cipient, ensuring that the light never dimmed. Each return was a testament to their shar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        ed future, a refusal to let the selfishness of the self consume the splendor of the whol) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        e. By tempering their gain, they wove the threads of trust into a tapestry that defied t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        he hunger of the void. Thus, they walked forward together, knowing that prosperity is no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        t found in accumulation, but in the rhythm of the gift returned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
