BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      Myth: The Bridge of Reciprocity was not built of stone or wood, but of the invisible threa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        ds of repeated promises. In the high altitudes of the Great Divide, Dorian and the Weave) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        r observed a chasm that separated potential from reality. To cross, one must relinquish ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        their hold on the five golden stones, casting them into the abyss where the winds of cha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        nce multiply them into a greater harvest. Yet, the bridge remains incomplete unless the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        one on the far side catches the bounty and offers a portion back to the source. It is a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        precarious architecture; it requires the Giver to risk everything with an open palm and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        the Receiver to recognize that individual gain is fleeting compared to the perpetual gro) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        wth of the bridge itself. If the Giver provides the full harvest of five, they are layin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        g the foundation. If the Receiver returns a generous portion, they are reinforcing the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        tructure. Together, they recognize that the game is not a battle of wits, but a collabor) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        ative design. Each iteration strengthens the path, ensuring that the cycle of trust tran) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        sforms the barren void into a bustling thoroughfare of shared prosperity, built to withs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        tand the winds of greed and the silence of isolation.) Tj ET
