BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (         not forged once, but rebuilt with every passing shadow. The travelers, having once cast) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (         their embers into the chasm and witnessed the miracle of multiplication, came to realiz) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        e that the chasm was not a gap to be crossed, but a vessel to be filled. The embers-five) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        , then fifteen-were not just currency; they were units of faith. To keep the fifteen for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (         oneself was to end the cycle, to let the bridge crumble into the darkness below. But to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (         return the half was to weave the glass anew, stronger and more resilient than before. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        s the travelers moved from side to side, alternating the roles of donor and recipient, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        he rhythmic pulse of their exchange became the heartbeat of the realm itself. They under) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        stood that the game was never about the size of the hoard, but the integrity of the cycl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        e. Every act of returning was a stitch in the fabric of their shared existence, binding ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        their futures together. In the end, they found that the bridge was not merely a path, bu) Tj ET
